simplify-cpp-comments: The pack body comment restates the declaration contract and the two loop bounds below it [nit].

Evidence, HEAD lines 133-135:
```
  // Writes columns 0..group_heads-1 of every panel; the remaining columns are
  // padding the caller keeps zero (see the contract at the declaration). One
  // panel per 32-dim step.
```

Rule 2 and Rule 4. "Writes columns 0..group_heads-1" is the loop `q_head < group_heads` (line 138). "One panel per 32-dim step" is the loop `step < HEAD_SIZE_128 / DIM_STEP_32` (line 136). "padding the caller keeps zero" is the contract at amx_attn_iface.hpp:192-197, which the comment already points to. Three comment lines above a ten-line body, each mapping to a loop bound or to the declaration.

Reading cost: the reader reads the loop bounds twice.

Proposed text (one line, keeping the pointer the file already uses):
```
