```

simplify-cpp-comments: The tile-geometry comment repeats Note [Tile stores write 16 rows] (the named comment block at lines 93-110) sentence by sentence [should-fix].

Evidence, HEAD lines 128-132:
```
// 8 tiles as 16 rows x 64 bytes. A tile store (TILESTORED) always writes all
// 16 rows, even when only group_heads of them hold real data (see Note [Tile
// stores write 16 rows]). Only one caller buffer receives a tile store
// directly: the output `o` of weights_times_v_128x4. The caller must
// therefore allocate `o` with TILE_ROWS_16 rows, not group_heads.
```

Rule 2 as written: "A comment does not repeat what names and types already say. A pointer to a Note is kept only when the Note holds a fact the names do not", and the self-check adds "No comment restates a name, a type, or a Note." The Note at lines 95-100 says each of these facts in the same order. The restatement predates the PR (BASE had it with "4"). The PR touches this comment, so this is the moment to shorten it. Two places now need the same edit at every shape change.

Proposed text (3 lines, the begin_region() fact is also at lines 89-90, so the comment could shrink to the pointer alone):
```
// Tile geometry shared by every kernel below: begin_region() configures all 8
// tiles as 16 rows x 64 bytes. A tile store writes all 16 rows. See Note [Tile
// stores write 16 rows].
```

simplify-cpp-comments: The shape-constants comment restates the constant names below it and the byte counts of Note [AMX attention dispatch] (the named comment block at the top of this header) [nit].

Evidence, HEAD lines 137-139:
```
// a 64-token KV page, 128-dim heads, and 4 or 16 query heads per KV head
// (4 x 128 bf16 = 1024 bytes per query group, 16 x 128 bf16 = 4096 bytes).
// The kernel's shape constants derive from these.
```

Rule 2 (do not restate identifiers or a Note). "64-token KV page, 128-dim heads, 4 or 16 query heads per KV head" is spelled by PAGE_TOKENS_64, HEAD_SIZE_128, GROUP_HEADS_4 and GROUP_HEADS_16 on lines 140-145. The byte counts are Note [AMX attention dispatch] lines 25-26. "derive from these" is visible in `Q_PACK_ELEMS_2048 = TILE_ROWS_16 * HEAD_SIZE_128` (line 158).

Reading cost: four lines that repeat the next ten lines of code.

Proposed text for lines 136-139 (one line):
```
