```

simplify-cpp-comments: The GROUP_HEADS_16 comment says what the static_assert message two lines below says [nit].

Evidence, HEAD lines 143-147:
```
// 16 heads fill the 16 packed-Q columns of the QK B tile and the 16 P rows of
// the PV A tile, so that group size needs no padding.
inline constexpr size_t GROUP_HEADS_16 = 16;
static_assert(GROUP_HEADS_16 == TILE_ROWS_16,
    "16 heads fill one tile's 16 rows (PV) and 16 columns (QK) exactly");
```

Rule 3: prefer an assert over a comment when one exists. The compiler checks the rows half (GROUP_HEADS_16 == TILE_ROWS_16). The columns half lives in the assert's message string, since the header defines no tile-column constant. Either way the comment adds nothing the assert does not carry.

Reading cost: the same fact read twice in five lines.

Proposed: delete lines 143-144 and keep the static_assert.

simplify-cpp-comments: The shape_ok comment restates the one-expression body below it [nit].

Evidence, HEAD lines 161-164:
```
// The shape half of the gate: the AMX kernels serve 128-dim heads with 4 or
// 16 query heads per KV head (see Note [AMX attention dispatch]).
constexpr bool shape_ok(size_t model_head_size, size_t model_kv_mul) noexcept {
  return model_head_size == HEAD_SIZE_128 && group_heads_ok(model_kv_mul);
```

Rule 1 (the name carries it) and Rule 2 (do not restate identifiers). "128-dim heads" is `HEAD_SIZE_128` on line 164. "4 or 16 query heads per KV head" is `group_heads_ok`, whose body at lines 152-154 reads `g == GROUP_HEADS_4 || g == GROUP_HEADS_16`. The same sentence also appears at lines 136-138, so it is in this header twice. The one fact left is that this is the shape half of `eligible` (line 178).

Reading cost: the reader reads the predicate twice.

Proposed text (one line):
```
// The shape half of the gate (see Note [AMX attention dispatch]).
```

simplify-cpp-comments: "For 16 heads every column is written, so that precondition is empty" restates the range group_heads..15 given two lines earlier [nit].

Evidence, HEAD lines 193-196:
```
// bytes, with columns group_heads..15 of every panel already zero: this call
// writes columns 0..group_heads-1 only, so a buffer zeroed once at allocation
// stays valid for every pack. For 16 heads every column is written, so that
// precondition is empty.
```

The skill's goal line (one fact per comment line that the code does not already say) and Rule 4 (a comment line that maps to no code line). For group_heads = 16 the range 16..15 is empty by reading. The static_assert at lines 146-147 and Note [AMX attention dispatch] at line 28 already keep the fact. The commit added the 16-heads clauses on purpose, so this is optional.

Reading cost: the reader checks whether the extra sentence changes the contract. It does not.

Proposed edit: line 195 becomes `// stays valid for every pack.` and line 196 is deleted.

Optional, pre-existing [fwiw]: lines 198-199 state the padding columns a second time inside the layout description ("(columns 0..group_heads-1 = the heads, the rest zero padding)"). BASE already had both statements. If touched, lines 192-194 can be the single owner and line 198 can read `// 16 dim-pair rows x 16 query columns x 2 paired values:`.

simplify-cpp-comments: "no padding for 16 heads" in Note [QK orientation] (this named comment block) is the third copy of the fact in this header [nit].

Evidence, HEAD lines 223-224:
```
//   as 16 columns (the heads first, then padding columns the caller keeps
//   zero; no padding for 16 heads) in the VNNI pair-interleaved layout, one
```

Rule 2 (restatement, the skill's self-check: no comment restates a name, a type, or a Note). The bullet already says "the heads first, then padding columns the caller keeps zero", and with group_heads = 16 the padding is zero columns. Line 28 says "(none for 16 heads)" and lines 195-196 say "For 16 heads every column is written". The pack contract (lines 192-199) owns the layout.

Reading cost: a reader meets the same aside three times and checks whether the three differ.

Proposed text for lines 222-225:
```
// - B operand = packed Q. The group_heads query heads of the group are packed
//   as 16 columns (the heads first, then padding columns the caller keeps
