simplify-cpp-comments: The resize() comment restates what the packer does instead of saying only why resize() satisfies the pack precondition [nit].

Evidence, HEAD lines 1552-1554:
```
        // resize() zero-fills new slots and the packer writes only the kv_mul
        // live columns of each slot, so the padding it relies on stays zero
        // (see the pack contract in amx_attn_iface.hpp).
```

Rule 5: a call-site comment says only why here, and what the callee does belongs to the callee's comment. "the packer writes only the kv_mul live columns" (kv_mul = query heads per KV head) is the pack contract at amx_attn_iface.hpp:193-194. The placement reason is that resize()'s zero-fill is the contract's precondition (padding columns already zero).

