```

simplify-cpp-comments: The s_pages comment repeats the static_assert's expression and message [nit].

Evidence, HEAD lines 1757-1762:
```
      // Both kernels take &s_pages[0][0] with row stride page_size, so the
      // kv_mul rows of 64 floats must be consecutive with no padding. The size
      // check forces both: kv_mul x 64 x 4 bytes leaves no room for a gap.
      static_assert(
          sizeof(s_pages) == operation_kv_mul * page::page_size * sizeof(float),
          "the AMX kernels read s_pages as one block: rows must be consecutive");
```

Rule 3 (prefer an assert over a comment) and Rule 2 (do not restate). "must be consecutive with no padding" is the assert message. "kv_mul x 64 x 4 bytes" (kv_mul = query heads per KV head) is the assert expression. The one fact the assert does not state is why it matters: both kernels take `&s_pages[0][0]` with row stride page_size.

Reading cost: the assert read three times, as prose, as expression and as message.

Proposed text for lines 1757-1759 (one line):
```
      // Both kernels take &s_pages[0][0] with row stride page_size.
```

simplify-cpp-comments: The query-fill comment says "exact in bf16" twice and restates the constant and the expression below it [nit].

Evidence, HEAD lines 142-146:
```
    // Each head carries its own offset (i / head_size), so a pack that
    // permutes or drops heads cannot pass; every value is exact in bf16. The
    // offset step is 1/16: head 15 gives at most 2.6875, exact in bf16.
    constexpr float HEAD_OFFSET_STEP_0_0625 = 0.0625f;
    expected[i] = 1.0f + static_cast<float>(i / head_size) * HEAD_OFFSET_STEP_0_0625 +
```

Rule 2 for "The offset step is 1/16" (the name HEAD_OFFSET_STEP_0_0625 carries 0.0625 = 1/16) and for "(i / head_size)" (line 146 computes it). Rule 4 and the one-fact-per-line goal for the repeated "exact in bf16" on lines 143 and 144. What survives: why each head gets its own offset, and that the largest value is exact in bf16. Verified: 1 + 15 * 0.0625 + 3 * 0.25 = 2.6875 = 1.01011b x 2^1, 5 fraction bits, inside bf16's 7.

Reading cost: three lines for two facts, with one fact given twice.

Proposed text for lines 142-144 (one edit covers both points):
```
    // A per-head offset makes the packer read every head from its own address:
    // a wrong start pointer or stride cannot pass. Every value is exact in bf16
    // (head 15 reaches 2.6875).
